Body:
@rekram1-node — gentle nudge in case this is in your queue. Same area as #25698 / #25591 which you've handled recently.

Status: CI green, all three review nits from `Bojun-Vvibe/oss-contributions` addressed in `27e44f9` (bounded `completedAssistantMessageIds`, timeout warn log + timer cleanup, regression test using existing `createFakeAgent` harness — `bun test test/acp/` 12 pass / 0 fail, typecheck clean).

This is a v2 of #25422 (auto-closed by the template bot 2h after open). Happy to rebase or split further if the diff shape isn't right.

@rekram1-node — would you have a moment when you're next in the ACP queue? Same area as the `end_turn` race fix in #25683 (still open, also pinging there) — both are about stopReason correctness on session/prompt completion.

This one returns `cancelled` rather than `end_turn` when the user cancels mid-turn, so ACP clients can distinguish a user-aborted turn from a clean completion. CI green, no conflicts. v2 of #25901 (template-bot auto-close).

Happy to add a regression test or reshape if anything's off.

@rekram1-node — opening this on your radar since you've been merging ACP-area PRs lately (#25698, #25591). Just filed the missing upstream issue (#26349) and updated the body to reference it.

This PR is **type-only / additive**: introduces an `AgentErrorUpdate` `session/update` kind so non-tool LLM failures (budget, rate limit, provider 5xx, context overflow, …) can surface as typed frames instead of looking like a stalled stream on the wire. Nothing in the codebase imports the new module yet — the actual emit at `halt()` is intentionally a separate change so the wire contract can land first.

CI green, `bun test test/acp/agent-error.test.ts` 12 pass. Happy to reshape the vocabulary or split further if anything's off.

My situation turned out to be not an issue with opencode but with the MCP provider. The provider said they were working on the issue, but suggested I rather use auth via a pat like this:

```json
"medusa": {
  "type": "remote",
  "url": "https://docs.medusajs.com/mcp",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {token}"
  },
  "oauth": false
}
```

I don't know that there is an issue with opencode here. My apologies, I meant to leave a comment when closing the issue.
